WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.568
First up,
he is the governor of Florida,

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.337
who is--
Wow! Currently on our show?

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.404
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.373
...currently running
to be the Republican nominee

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.075
for president in 2024,

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:10.309
Governor Ron DeSantis!

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.313
(AUDIENCE CHEERS, APPLAUDS)

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.114
-Hey!
-What's up, man?

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.282
-Ron.
-How are you doing?

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.550
That's a pretty dark blue state
right there.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.784
I know, I know.
Welcome back.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:19.886
That's not bad.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.656
All right.
On a scale of nine to ten,

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.224
what'd you think
of my monologue?

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.559
Honestly, I was laughing.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.727
-I'll give you that.
-Right?

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.996
Laughing on both sides of
the aisle too, so it was good.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.264
And welcome back to the show.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.799
I know you guys
were on hiatus for a while.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.800
Oh, thank you.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.767
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:35.869
(CHUCKLES) Yes.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.504
I-- I do gotta put in a plug.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.706
Like, if you ever have problems
in California,

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:41.841
you know, in Florida,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.542
not only do we have
no income tax,

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.978
no vax mandates allowed
in the state of Florida.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.847
Well, we're gonna get to that.
We're gonna get to that.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.082
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.918
I know. But people do
wear cowboy boots with a suit.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:53.920
-RON DESANTIS: That's right.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.656
So, I'm not going to Florida.
Okay? That's--

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.657
That's just a crazy thing.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.225
We're proud of it.
We're proud of it.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.595
But there were no cowboys
in Florida, Ron.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.096
No, yeah.
You should try Florida.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.432
We're one of the top
cattle states in America.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.766
-BILL MAHER: Really?
-Once you go from the beach,

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.037
you go to the interior Florida,
nothing but cattle ranches.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.740
Oh, all right.
Well, I-- (CHUCKLES)

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.041
I stand corrected.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.010
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.811
Because I'm wearing
orthopedic shoes.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:19.913
There you go.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:20.980
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.682
Okay, so the debate.
It was a shit show.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.151
But I-- Right?

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.719
I mean, even you said
you wouldn't have--

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.688
you would have turned it off
if you were watching.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.323
I mean, people screaming
over each other.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.324
I couldn't hear what
any of them were saying.
It was terrible.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:33.492
But I heard you won.

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.027
I heard the polling
said you won.

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.497
-What did you win? With--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.464
No, honestly.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.133
With Trump not in the race,
what did you win?

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.834
Well, but I think that,
you know,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.104
he-- he's not showing up,
he's missing in action.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.173
He owes it to voters
to show up

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:48.408
and defend his record.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.010 line:0%
And I think he thinks
he can take a juiced poll

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.077 line:0%
and then people
don't get to vote.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.579 line:0%
That's not the way
the system works.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:54.647 line:0%
You gotta go earn votes.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.715 line:0%
So I'm showing up,
I'm showing that--

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.750 line:0%
And that's--
Here's the thing.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.786 line:0%
In the midst of all the show
that happened,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.787
I was the one guy
that people said,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.123
"You know what?
This guy's actually acting
like a president,"

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.324
when the rest were not.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.893
And so, okay, there I am.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.995
I told Donald,
"Let's do a debate."

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.530
I'm debating your governor,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.131
-Gavin Newsom, soon.
-BILL: We're gonna get to that.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:13.933
But let's do a debate
with me and him.

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:15.100
-I'll do it.
-BILL: Okay. All right.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.403
But this--
Can I ask you one thing
about these debates?

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.305
Can you get rid of this guy,
Doug Burgum?

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.075
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.843
This guy-- (CHUCKLES)
This bugs me.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.311
He is not gonna be president.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.580
This guy could start dating
Taylor Swift,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.514
no one would care.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.818
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:36.655
North Dakota, it's not
even a state. All right.

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.526
But you know, the thing is,
you did not take my advice.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:40.760
What was it?

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.996
I was on this show a few times
and we talked about it.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.865
I said, "This guy's crazy
to run this time. He's--"

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.267
-What are you, 45 years old?
-Yeah.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.467
-You just had a birthday, right?
-Yeah.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.136
You could run
for the next 20 years.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.871
If you were Biden, the next 40.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.606
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:54.706 --> 00:02:56.976
Okay, why run against Trump?

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.811
You're trying
to thread this needle

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:00.212
that will never happen.

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:01.380
Well, for a couple reasons.

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:03.549
You can't--
You can't disavow him,

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.284
because that's the base,

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.153
and yet you're running
against him.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.688
And that's why--
I mean, let's face it, Ron.

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.590
If this-- If the campaign
was going well,

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:12.858
you wouldn't be on this show.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:15.294
-Oh, that's not true.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.531
So, um, one, I don't think
he can win the election.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.299
Uh, I could win the election.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:23.369
Two, I don't think he could
actually get the job done
that we need to do.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:25.004
For example, COVID.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.739
I think we need accountability

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.941
for what this government did
to this country

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.710
with the COVID restrictions,
mandates, and lockdowns.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.446
Donald Trump
is not gonna do that.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.413
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.348
He says he did everything right.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.051
He says he saved millions
of lives with lockdowns.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.954
He claims his mRNA shots
saved 100 million lives.

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:45.658
He's not gonna clean house
at CDC, NIH, FDA,
or any of that.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.493
I will do that.
I will get the job done.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:48.694
And a lot of other things we do.

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:50.096
The one thing about me
in Florida,

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.764
and even my critics
will acknowledge,

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.599
if he says
he's gonna do something,

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.568
he will follow through
and get the job done.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.636
So it's about the country.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.205
Are we gonna get the country
turned around or not?

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.407
I don't think he's a vehicle
that-- that's doing it.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.809
And-- And I have been--

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:06.045
When I supported him on the
things I liked, I've said it,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.981
but I've been critical about
the things that he didn't do.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.116
And I'll continue to do that.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.217
Okay, but you--

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:15.755
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:20.359
But you campaigned for--
for election deniers in 2022.

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:22.161
This I do not forgive.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.197
-Well, look--
-To quote<i> The Godfather.</i>

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.631
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.466
I mean, Kari Lake,

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.136
who said Biden
is an illegitimate president,

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.938
-Trump didn't--
-Well, now she's attacking me,

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.540
so maybe I did
make a mistake there

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.874
'cause she's out there saying--

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:39.278
she's trying to say that
we mandated vax in Florida,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.246
when we did the opposite.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.848
We protected people
even from private mandates,

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.216
so-- so that may have been--

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:45.484
But Trump lost the election,
right?

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.920
-RON: Yeah, yeah.
-Okay, so why did you campaign
for people who said--

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.723
Because I wanted to see
Republicans win key races.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.691
I think it's important to have--

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.059
And that's not
a deal-breaker issue for you?

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.160
That's not democracy?

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.695
Well, okay.
Well, let's go back to 2016.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:59.131
Uh, you're friends in Hollywood
were cutting ads

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:02.535
telling the electoral college
to vote against Trump

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.803
in the electoral college
because it was stolen.

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.906 line:0%
They said Russia
stole the election.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.474 line:0%
For years, they said that.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.543 line:0%
So don't act like
this is, like, a unique thing

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.911 line:0%
in modern history
of the country.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:16.949 line:0%
-BILL: First--
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:19.485
First of all, Ron,
I have no friends in Hollywood.

